#ntdiff PUBLIC/OAK/BIN/REGISTRY.INI
#crlf
=1 1 11
+// The R3000 port (the DECstation 5000/200): a workgroup, and the           //
+// Password logs the first run on by itself.                                //
=1 14 4
=1 30 10
=1 50 8
+    DECSTATION
=1 74 9
+    Administrator
+
+;
+;  The R3000 port: the password of that account.  winlogon.cmd sets
+;  AutoAdminLogon and DefaultPassword: from the third boot on, NT logs the
+;  account on by itself (Shift held down while NT starts shows the Welcome
+;  box).  Without a password winlogon.cmd waits for a key.
+;
+
+Password
+    password
=1 84 6
+
+Environment
+    tmp = c:\tmp
=1 183 14
=1 221 37
=1 424 21
+;  The R3000 port: the workgroup of the machine.  A DomainId would make
+;  it a member of the domain, which the first run joins (netjoin).
=1 444 4
+    WORKGROUP
=1 452 24
=1 30 2
+;  The R3000 port: commands for winlogon.cmd, a ! puts one at its end.  In a
+;  workgroup winlogon.cmd runs ADDUSER, which only makes new accounts: NET USER
+;  gives the account above its password.
+;
+
+InsertScript
+    !net user Administrator password
